rface. L64: cite14†New Mexico Lawyer Fined $5,000 After Using ChatGPT to Draft Murder Appeal With Fake Witnesses L65: \nL66: A New Mexico defense lawyer has been fined $5,000 after using ChatGPT to help draft a murder appeal, failing to check what it produced and filing a brief that included four witnesses who never existed, false testimony, and misrepresented legal authority.The New Mexico Supreme Court held Santa Fe attorney Stephen... cite14†Read More » L67: \nL68: Legal Blogs\nL69: cite15†Image: Hands analyzing financial charts and a digital asset allocation graphic above stacks of coins. L70: \nL71: cite16†The Role of Private Investigators in Asset Searches for Litigation†www.miausa.com L72: \nL73: by Millennium Intelligence Agency | Investigative Services\nL74: \nL75: Attorney Advertising\nL76: ## Law Commentary\nL77: \nL78:   * cite17†About Us†info.lawcommentary.com L79:   * cite18†Privacy Policy†info.lawcommentary.com L80:   * cite19†Copyright Policy†info.lawcommentary.com L81:   * cite20†Contact Us†info.lawcommentary.com L82: \nL83: ## For Lawyers\nL84: \nL85:   * cite21†Showcase Your Law Firm Blog†info.lawcommentary.com L86:   * cite22†Be a Legal Commentator†info.lawcommentary.com L87:   * cite23†Advertise Your Law Firm†info.lawcommentary.com L88: ## Publishers and News Agencies\nL89: \nL90:   * cite24†Our Legal News Content†info.lawcommentary.com L91:   * cite25†Licensing Agreement†info.lawcommentary.com L92:   * cite26†Syndication Feeds L93: \nL94: ## Follow Law Commentary\nL95: \nL96:   *   *   *   *   * © 2020 - 2026 Law Commentary, LLC. All rights reserved.\nL97: \nL98: ## Search articles and Legalpedia\nL99: \nL100: Search articles and Legalpedia [Input: Search articles and Legalpedia] [Button: Search ]\nL101: \nL102: ## Subscribe to Newsletter\nL103: \nL104: cite27†Newsletter signup form†40faf09e.sibforms.com --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error